Package: plugin-qualification-records
Architecture: amd64 arm64
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${qualify:Depends}
Provides: ${records:Provides}
Replaces: ${records:Replaces}
Breaks: ${records:Breaks}
Description: plugin-db qualification layer: records of OpenMixer plugin sets
 The qualification layer of the plugin database: the plugin-qualify records
 of the plugin sets measured on a reference machine of a host class.
 plugin-qualify-sync takes a plugin from them instead of measuring it, and
 only when every file of the installed plugin hashes as the measured one
 did; any other plugin is measured on the machine as before. The sync
 chooses the set of the machine's class and cell.
 .
 Each architecture carries the sets of its machine classes:
 .
  arm64: the rpi5 class, the zynthian-vangelis set measured on a Raspberry
  Pi 5 with ZynthianOS. Hardware records: measured on the machine's own
  audio interface; the verdicts hold, the figures describe that interface
  and are not compared with the reference tier.
 .
  amd64: the x86-64 class, the fedora44 sets, one per sample rate and
  quantum. Provisional records: measured on JACK's dummy driver without
  real-time priority; the crash, hang and unmeasured verdicts hold, the
  cost, latency and xrun figures are not reference figures.

Package: libplugin-qualification-db0
Section: libs
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, libsqlite3-0 (>= 3.37.0), libomx-domain0 (>= 3.20.0)
Description: reader of the OpenMixer qualification store
 The C library that reads the qualification store: the base database of
 plugin-qualification-records and a user layer, merged by whole record, with
 every word column checked against the contract domains that own its words.
 It reads figures at start-up, never in a real-time path.

Package: libplugin-qualification-db-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: libplugin-qualification-db0 (= ${binary:Version}), ${misc:Depends}
Description: reader of the OpenMixer qualification store, development files
 The header, the shared library link, plugin-qualification-db.pc and the DDL
 of the store (the pkg-config variable schema names it).

Package: plugin-qualification-db
Section: sound
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: command to query the OpenMixer qualification store
 plugin-qualification-db query --json prints the results of the base
 database and the user layer, one JSON object per line; check opens both
 layers and the words they hold.
